 "text": "-->\nTREASURER | Chippewa County\ntop of page\nSkip to Main Content\nChippewa\nCounty,\nMichigan\nHOME\nDEPARTMENTS\nADMINISTRATOR'S OFFICE\nBOARD OF COMMISSIONERS\nBUILDING DEPARTMENT\nCLERK\nDRAIN COMMISSION\nEQUALIZATION\nHEALTH DEPARTMENT\nINFORMATION SYSTEMS\nMEDICAL EXAMINER\nMSU EXTENSION\nREGISTER OF DEEDS\nSURVEYOR\nTREASURER\nVeteran Affairs\nLAW & JUSTICE\n50TH CIRCUIT COURT\n91ST DISTRICT COURT\n17th Probate Court\nANIMAL SHELTER\nEMERGENCY 911\nFRIEND OF THE COURT\nJUVENILE COURT\nPROSECUTING ATTORNEY\nPUBLIC DEFENDER\nSHERIFF'S OFFICE\nRELATED SITES\nCHIPPEWA COUNTY INTERNATIONAL AIRPORT\nCOMMUNITY ACTION\nCONSERVATION DISTRICT\nCommunity Mediation Services\nEUP REGIONAL PLANNING\nEUP TRANSPORTATION AUTHORITY\nHIAWATHA BEHAVIORAL HEALTH\nMICHIGAN WORKS\nMSU EXTENSION\nNORTHERN TRANSITIONS\nROAD COMMISSION\nTOWNSHIPS\nHOW DO I.....\nAPPLY FOR:\nBUILDING PERMIT\nBOARD & COMMITTEE SEAT\nBUSINESS LICENSE\nCONCEALED WEAPONS PERMIT\nDOG LICENSE\nDISABLED VETERAN'S TAX EXEMPTION\nFIND:\nFOIA POLICY\nELECTION RESULTS\nPROPERTY TAX INFORMATION\nBID POSTINGS\nREQUEST:\nBIRTH CERTIFICATE\nCOURT RECORDS\nDEATH RECORDS\nMARRIAGE LICENSE\nPASSPORTS\nPROPERTY INFORMATION\nMore\nUse tab to navigate through the menu items.\nHelpful Links\nFAQs\n​\nForeclosure Timeline\n​\nForeclosure Excess Proceeds\n​\nAuction Pamphlet\n​\nOnline Payments\n​\nHardship Extension Policy\n​\n​ Summer Deferment Form\n​\n​\nContact Information\n319 Court Street\nSault Ste. Marie, MI 49783\nPhone:(906) 635-6308\n​\n​\nCounty Treasurer\nOffice Hours:\nMonday - Friday 8:00am to 5:00pm (except holidays)\n​\nTreasurer:\nJenni Pace\n​\n*All tax information must be obtained over the phone, not through e-mail.\nDelinquent Tax Records\nChippewa County Delinquent Tax Records are available online and are free at this time.\nEvery effort has been made to ensure the accuracy and completeness of the information provided. Chippewa County makes no warranty expressed or implied, regarding errors or omissions and assumes no liability or responsibility for improper or incorrect information or data described and/or contained within this website.\n​\n​\nTo determine your balance due, access the Delinquent Real Property Tax Records by clicking here.\n​\nOnce you have looked up your delinquent real property tax information, or if you already know the amount due, click below to pay using a debit or credit card. This service is offered through GovPay. Gov Pay will assess a 3% fee with a minimum of $3.99 on credit cards, and a flat fee of $3.95 on debit cards. Click here to make an online payment.\n​\nOverview\nElected to a four-year term, the County Treasurer serves as the custodian of all County funds, and as such is responsible for receipting, recording and investing all money deposited with the County. The Treasurer is also responsible for maintaining debt service accounts for all the bonded indebtedness of the County.\n​\nBeginning March 1st of each year the Treasurer collects delinquent real property taxes and following an extensive notification title work process a court order is issued which allows for the sale of properties which are more than 24 months delinquent. The County Treasurer also serves as the agent of the delinquent tax revolving fund, through which the County is able to forward to local units the amount of delinquent taxes due and owing on real property.\nThe Treasurer is responsible for the certification of deeds and other real estate title transfers prior to recording the documents.\nThe Treasurer is a member of the Plat Board, the Elections Commission, the County Allocation Board and the County Economic Development Corporation.\n​\nbottom of page",
